# Desktop / game macros

This workspace (and later PackMacro-style tools) automates **games** (Roblox, etc.). Follow these so we do not relearn the same bugs.

## Mouse (always)

- **Never** use `pyautogui.moveTo` / `SetCursorPos` as the way the **game** sees the cursor. The OS pointer moves; Roblox and many games ignore it until the user moves a physical mouse.
- Use **Windows `SendInput` relative moves** plus **left `MOUSEEVENTF_LEFTDOWN` / `LEFTUP`** (see `DesktopMacroProject/raw_mouse.py`). Slide on X and Y, hover, then click.
- Only log `LIVE click` after `GetCursorPos` is near the target **and** the left button packets were sent.
- Do not click if the cursor is not already on the **game monitor**. Do not teleport.
- Never click the **window Close (X)** or title bar. In-game overlay X only (dark Join Event style). Windowed (not exclusive fullscreen) must keep working.

## Keys

- Default Start/Stop hotkey is **`=`** (equals), global, works while the game is focused. Keep it configurable in the UI.
- Game claim/buy may still use `E` as an in-game key.

## UI / exe

- Prefer windowed builds (no extra CMD). Do not kill/relaunch the app on every tiny tweak.
- One-file PyInstaller on Python 3.14 has crashed with `Failed to import encodings module`. Prefer `python main.py` for local testing if the exe is broken.

## Scope

Apply whenever adding macros, clicks, hotkeys, or overlay tools in this repo or a sibling `*Macro*` folder.
